Hi Nick,

I have a similar issue. Everything is now working fine are re-installing from GitHub last week (no scary errors). I set ncores=8 and I am running from terminal. I can see that there are 8 R threads, however one R is using 98%+ of CPU time and the other 7 only ~1% each. I think this is related to the analysis running very slowly for me after the update. Do you have any suggestions? Thank you!

On Thursday, November 15, 2018 at 3:16:32 PM UTC-7, Nick Matzke wrote:
> I should have added, time-stratification slows things down also, because (1) the tree is chopped up by time-bin, resulting in many more branches and more matrix exponentiations, and (2) efficient parallelization is harder to do for time-stratified analyses.
>
> Cheers!
> Nick
