> > > > > >  It seems like everything now runs fine, but for the time. Its over 20 hours since istarted running the DIVALIKE and it is not yet complete. But the DEC and DEC+J were pretty fast. Don´t know what could be the problem. Because I ran these same analyses using the same computer and it never took this long.
> > > > > >
> > > > > >
> > > > > >
> > > > > > 1. I am trying to rerun the analysis without the +j parameter (Reviewer´s suggestion). The DIVALIKE is the most appropriate model in this case. However, I have followed the updated version of BioBeoBears and now everything runs fine up to DEC +J. I am interested in DIVALIKE and calculating the probability per node, but since this analysis (DIVALIKE) has been running for more than  20 hours and not yet finished. I do not know how long i still have to wait for the calculations to be completed.
> > > > > >
> > > > > > Could you please run these analyses for me, probably you have a better computer which might be one of the reasons for such a slow run.
> > > > > >
> > > > > >
> > > > > >
